            <ArticleTitle>Chest wall resection and reconstruction for Rosai-Dorfman disease masquerading as a chest wall sarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1-e3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/rcsann.2017.0199</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rosai-Dorfman disease (RDD) is a rare benign histiocytic proliferative disease that can present as a pseudotumour of soft tissue. We describe the first chest wall resection and reconstruction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
